---
import "../../styles/global.css";
import SiteNav from "../../components/SiteNav.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import DocsSidebar from "../../components/DocsSidebar.astro";
import { siteUrl } from "../../content/site-links";

const pageTitle = "OpenRemote Getting Started";
const pageDescription = "Connect OpenRemote to OpenCode, discover servers, scan QR codes, and start using sessions from your phone.";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="description" content={pageDescription} />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#151718" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="OpenRemote" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="article" />
    <meta property="og:url" content={`${siteUrl}/docs/getting-started`} />
    <meta property="og:title" content={pageTitle} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={pageDescription} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={`${siteUrl}/og-image.jpg`} />
    <meta property="og:image:type" content="image/jpeg" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content={pageTitle} />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content={pageDescription} />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content={`${siteUrl}/og-image.jpg`} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={`${siteUrl}/docs/getting-started`} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/openremote-icon.svg" />
    <title>{pageTitle}</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <input id="docs-menu-toggle" class="docs-menu-toggle" type="checkbox" aria-hidden="true" />
    <SiteNav docsMenu />
    <label class="docs-menu-backdrop" for="docs-menu-toggle" aria-label="Close docs navigation"></label>

    <main class="page-shell docs-page-shell">
      <div class="docs-layout">
        <DocsSidebar />

        <article class="docs-content">
          <header class="docs-header">
            <h1>Connect OpenRemote to OpenCode</h1>
            <p>Start OpenCode on your computer, open OpenRemote on your phone, then connect over your local network.</p>
          </header>

          <section class="guide-section">
            <h2>Connect from OpenRemote</h2>
            <div class="install-tabs getting-started-tabs" aria-label="OpenRemote connection options">
              <input id="connect-plugin" class="install-radio" type="radio" name="connect-path" data-connect-hash="with-plugin" checked />
              <input id="connect-lan" class="install-radio" type="radio" name="connect-path" data-connect-hash="without-plugin" />

              <div class="install-tab-list connect-tab-list" role="tablist" aria-label="Choose connection path">
                <label class="install-tab connect-tab-plugin" for="connect-plugin" role="tab">with OpenRemote plugin</label>
                <label class="install-tab connect-tab-lan" for="connect-lan" role="tab">without plugin</label>
              </div>

              <article class="install-panel connect-panel-plugin" role="tabpanel">
                <p>Install the <a class="inline-link" href="/docs/plugin">OpenRemote plugin</a>, then:</p>
                <pre><code>opencode --hostname 127.0.0.1</code></pre>
                <p class="scan-qr-note">Scan the QR code from OpenRemote.</p>
              </article>

              <article class="install-panel connect-panel-lan" role="tabpanel">
                <p class="lan-start-note">You can use the OpenRemote app without the plugin with most functionality:</p>
                <div class="command-options">
                  <pre><code>opencode --mdns</code></pre>
                  <span>or</span>
                  <pre><code>opencode --hostname 0.0.0.0</code></pre>
                </div>
              </article>

              <div class="doc-card password-note-panel">
                <h3 class="doc-subheading">Secure OpenCode before using shared or public Wi-Fi.</h3>
                <p>Newer versions of OpenCode allow <code>OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD</code> with LAN startup. The <a class="inline-link" href="/docs/plugin">OpenRemote plugin</a> is still recommended for QR setup, gateway registration, and OpenRemote proxy features.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <ul class="guide-list">
              <li>OpenRemote searches for OpenCode servers on your network.</li>
              <li>Tap a discovered server to fill the connection details.</li>
              <li>If discovery is unavailable, enter the host LAN IP and port, usually <code>4096</code>.</li>
              <li>On an Android emulator, connect to the host machine with <code>10.0.2.2:4096</code>.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section class="guide-section">
            <h2>Use OpenRemote</h2>
            <ul class="guide-list">
              <li>Browse and resume OpenCode sessions.</li>
              <li>Send chat prompts from your phone.</li>
              <li>Run shell commands and view output in the transcript.</li>
              <li>Approve or reject permission prompts remotely.</li>
              <li>Switch Build or Plan and choose connected models.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
          <SiteFooter docs />
        </article>
      </div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
